From: Victor Fuentes <victor@vlinkz.dev>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] firmware: arm_scmi: qcom: add the generic extension protocol and memlat devfreq
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The live Gen5 kernel already runs LLCC, DDR and DDR_QOS DVFS from
the CPUCP memlat governor: its config enables QCOM_SCMI_GENERIC_EXT
and SCMI_QCOM_MEMLAT_DEVFREQ, and its Kaanapali DT carries the
cpucp mailbox, the SCMI shared-memory window and the scmi-1
instance with vendor protocol@80.  The unified 7.2.6 tree has none
of that, so this is existing-function parity, not a new feature.

Rebase the original eight-patch series without redesign:

- the SCMI QCOM generic extension protocol documentation, binding,
  vendor implementation and client header;
- the devfreq target_freq attribute flag, the track_remote flag,
  the remote observer governor and the SCMI QCOM memlat driver that
  configures and starts the CPUCP algorithm and exposes one devfreq
  device per bus;
- the Kaanapali cpucp mailbox, cpucp SRAM window and cpucp_scmi:
  scmi-1 node with protocol@80.

The memlat driver binds only the Qualcomm vendor protocol 0x80 and
the Kaanapali compatible, so enabling it does not change other
boards.  The existing PDP0 SCMI instance (firmware SCMI at
17610000) and the CPU cpufreq path are untouched; PDP0 is not
replaced.

